{"c": null, "r": "I'm designing a Bank class where each instance maintains its own accounts dictionary. The open_account method validates that the account doesn't already exist and the initial balance is non-negative, while deposit requires a positive amount.

For withdraw, I need to validate the account exists and the amount is positive, then check if there are sufficient funds before deducting. Transfer validates both accounts exist, they're different, and the amount is positive, plus checks the source account has enough balance. I'm ordering validations so that positive amount checks happen first for consistency across all operations, and I'm ensuring that any operation that raises an exception leaves all balances unchanged.
", "t": [["write_file", "{"path":"D:\\Projects\\local_ai\\strata-lab\\runs\\work\\hermes\\bank-1794053343\\bank.py","content":"\"\"\"Account helpers. Balances are integer cents.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass InsufficientFunds(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when a withdrawal or transfer exceeds the source balance.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass Bank:\n    \"\"\"A set of named accounts with integer-cent balances.\n\n    Each Bank owns its own accounts; two instances never share them.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._accounts = {}\n\n    def open_account(self, name, initial=0):\n        if initial < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"initial must be >= 0: %r\" % (initial,))\n        if name in self._accounts:\n            raise ValueError(\"account exists: \" + name)\n        self._accounts[name] = initial\n\n    def deposit(self, name, amount):\n        if amount <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"amount must be > 0: %r\" % (amount,))\n        self._require(name)\n        self._accounts[name] += amount\n\n    def withdraw(self, name, amount):\n        if amount <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"amount must be > 0: %r\" % (amount,))\n        current = self._require(name)\n        if current < amount:\n            raise InsufficientFunds(\n                \"account %r has %d, cannot withdraw %d\" % (name, current, amount))\n        self._accounts[name] = current - amount\n\n    def balance(self, name):\n        return self._require(name)\n\n    def transfer(self, src, dst, amount):\n        if amount <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"amount must be > 0: %r\" % (amount,))\n        if src == dst:\n            raise ValueError(\"cannot transfer to the same account: \" + str(src))\n        src_balance = self._require(src)\n        dst_balance = self._require(dst)\n        if src_balance < amount:\n            raise InsufficientFunds(\n                \"account %r has %d, cannot transfer %d\" % (src, src_balance, amount))\n        self._accounts[src] = src_balance - amount\n        self._accounts[dst] = dst_balance + amount\n\n    def _require(self, name):\n        try:\n            return self._accounts[name]\n        except KeyError:\n            raise KeyError(\"unknown account: \" + str(name))\n\n\ndefault_bank = Bank()\n\n\ndef open_account(name, initial=0):\n    default_bank.open_account(name, initial)\n\n\ndef deposit(name, amount):\n    default_bank.deposit(name, amount)\n\n\ndef withdraw(name, amount):\n    default_bank.withdraw(name, amount)\n\n\ndef balance(name):\n    return default_bank.balance(name)\n\n\ndef transfer(src, dst, amount):\n    default_bank.transfer(src, dst, amount)\n"}"]]}

